// Title: NTDS Exfiltration Filename Patterns
// Sigma ID: 3a8da4e0-36c1-40d2-8b29-b3e890d5172a
// Status: test | Level: high
// Author: Florian Roth (Nextron Systems)
// Date: 2022-03-11 | Modified: 2023-05-05
// ATT&CK: credential-access, T1003.003
// Description: Detects creation of files with specific name patterns seen used in various tools that export the
//   NTDS.DIT for exfiltration.
// False positives:
//   - Unknown
// References:
//   - https://github.com/rapid7/metasploit-framework/blob/eb6535009f5fdafa954525687f09294918b5398d/modules/post/windows/gather/ntds_grabber.rb
//   - https://github.com/rapid7/metasploit-framework/blob/eb6535009f5fdafa954525687f09294918b5398d/data/post/powershell/NTDSgrab.ps1
//   - https://github.com/SecureAuthCorp/impacket/blob/7d2991d78836b376452ca58b3d14daa61b67cb40/impacket/examples/secretsdump.py#L2405
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/adf5a626c4a776f3f023056f0f398b9523a2f09e/rules/windows/file/file_event/file_event_win_ntds_exfil_tools.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language 12.4.1, live Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceFileEvents
| where FolderPath endswith "\\All.cab" or FolderPath endswith ".ntds.cleartext"
